#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0703 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: BASETYPE is not present, ByIND is populated, and ByIND is not equal to AyIND where ABLFL is equal to Y for a given value of PARAMCD for a combination of device and subject
#note "Same shape as the invalid sibling with B1IND=HIGH == A1IND=HIGH on the ABLFL=Y row -> noViolation. Restored by Fix #152: until the AyIND token was expanded, max(AyIND) read an absent column and the comparison fired here too."
dataset ADLBC class=MD-BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col SPDEVID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col ABLFL type=Char
col B1IND type=Char
col A1IND type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | DEV01 | GLUC | Y | HIGH | HIGH
---
